.TH SNCFGEDIT 8 "May 2017" "Xsan File System"
.SH NAME
sncfgedit \- Edit Xsan Volume configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
.nh
.HP
.B sncfgedit -n
.I VolName
.RB [ -f \ \fIFailedTemporaryConfigFile\fP]
.HP
.B sncfgedit -h
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBsncfgedit\fR program provides convenient method to edit the
Xsan file system configuration file for the named file system
and validate the new configuration file before overwriting the old
one.  To do so, \fBsncfgedit\fR creates a temporary copy of the
configuration file, and then opens it in an editor.
.PP
\fBsncfgedit\fR uses the the EDITOR environment variable to choose the
program used to edit the configuration file, or \fBvi\fR if EDITOR is
not set.
.PP
Validation includes standalone validation of the new configuration
file as well as validation of changes between original configuration
file and edited file if a configuration file previously existed.
If no previous configuration file exists, a template will be loaded
into the editor using default settings for all values.
.PP
Before an existing configuration file is overwritten, it is copied to
.I /Library/Logs/Xsan/data/\fRVolName\fP/config_history/
for future reference.  A
timestamp is appended to the filename to allow for the existence of
multiple backup copies.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-h\fR
Display usage.
.IP "\fB\-n \fIVolName\fR"
Required. The name of the file system whose config is to be edited or created.
.IP "\fB\-f \fIFailedTemporaryConfigFile\fR"
Specify the path to the temporary config file from a previous run
where the proposed changes were disallowed. This gives you another
chance without throwing away all of the previous changes.
.SH EXIT VALUES
\fBsncfgedit\fR will return 0 on success and non-zero on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B EDITOR
Allows the user to choose which editor is used to modify the
configuration file.  (default: vi)
.SH FILES
.I /Library/Logs/Xsan/data/\fRVolName\fP/config_history/*
